      "section": "GENERATOR SET OPERATION",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5654,
        "t": 712.3641068359375,
        "r": 291.39580000000024,
        "b": 677.1639492035388
      },
      "content": "Refer  to  Figures  5-3  and  5-4,  the  generator  set schematics, while working through the following description.",
      "hyperlink_hint": true,
      "section_id": "sec_auto_330",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_5",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_5",
          "title": "5. Generator Set/Voltage Regulator"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_330",
          "title": "GENERATOR SET OPERATION"
        }
      ],
      "page": 27,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0319",
      "reading_order": 332,
      "section": "GENERATOR SET OPERATION",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 55.8429,
        "t": 666.1036068359375,
        "r": 291.5520000000005,
        "b": 542.407349203539
      },
      "content": "Voltage  regulator  VR1  (three-phase:  VR21) supplies DC to the field winding (F1 - F2 leads) through brushes and slip rings, thereby establishing a revolving 4-pole magnetic field.  The battery is connected during startup to initiate field excitation.  Voltage regulator VR1 supplies field  current  during  operation.    Rated  output voltage is maintained as the generator set load varies, by varying field current to maintain field strength proportional to the load.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_330",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_5",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_5",
          "title": "5. Generator Set/Voltage Regulator"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_330",
          "title": "GENERATOR SET OPERATION"
        }
      ],
      "page": 27,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0320",
      "reading_order": 333,
      "section": "GENERATOR SET OPERATION",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 55.84289999999997,
        "t": 534.9176068359377,
        "r": 291.62679999999966,
        "b": 499.6602492035389
      },
      "content": "The revolving magnetic field induces AC in the stator windings (T1 - T2 and T3  - T4) which are connected to the load.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_330",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_5",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_5",
          "title": "5. Generator Set/Voltage Regulator"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_330",
          "title": "GENERATOR SET OPERATION"
        }
      ],
      "page": 27,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0321",
      "reading_order": 334,
      "section": "GENERATOR SET OPERATION",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 55.84289999999997,
        "t": 492.17160683593767,
        "r": 291.5619,
        "b": 456.97144920353895
      },
      "content": "Under light load, the stator windings can supply sufficient current for the field to maintain rated output voltage.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_330",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_5",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_5",
          "title": "5. Generator Set/Voltage Regulator"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_330",
          "title": "GENERATOR SET OPERATION"
        }
      ],
      "page": 27,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0322",
      "reading_order": 335,
      "section": "GENERATOR SET OPERATION",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 55.84289999999997,
        "t": 449.4828068359377,
        "r": 291.3980000000003,
        "b": 426.924949203539
      },
      "content": "As the load increases, load currents increase, resulting in a proportional increase of current,",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_330",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_5",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_5",
          "title": "5. Generator Set/Voltage Regulator"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_330",
          "title": "GENERATOR SET OPERATION"
        }
      ],
      "page": 27,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0323",
      "reading_order": 336,
      "section": "GENERATOR SET OPERATION",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 342.5392,
        "t": 737.9930068359378,
        "r": 564.7545999999996,
        "b": 702.792849203539
      },
      "content": "which in turn supplies the field.  Rated output voltage is thereby maintained as the load varies.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_330",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_5",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_5",
          "title": "5. Generator Set/Voltage Regulator"
        },
